\title{likingInitiative: the Liking Rating Database in R}
\description{
Subjective liking ratings from published decision-making studies.
}
\details{
Data is read from versioned release files and cached locally, so a pinned
version returns the same rows however long from now, and analyses keep
working when the web service does not.

Two things to get right:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Cross-study comparisons must use \code{normalized_rating}.} Response scales
differ between studies (0-4, 1-100, 1-870, willingness-to-pay in
dollars), so raw \code{rating} values are not comparable.
\code{normalized_rating} is \code{(rating - scale_min) / (scale_max - scale_min)}
and always lies in 0-1.
\item \strong{Subject ids are unique only within a dataset.} Subject \code{"12"} in two
datasets is two different people; key on \code{dataset_code} and \code{subject_id}
together.
}
